From d19f5444f8a6919336a7a5f650bc45f38d863324 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 15:16:52 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/22] input: usb_kbd_hid: treat -ETIMEDOUT like -EAGAIN
 during steady-state polling

usb_kbd_poll() called usb_kbd_release_all_keys() for any negative
do_poll() result, before checking whether that result was -EAGAIN.
-ETIMEDOUT got no such exemption at all: it fell through past the
-EAGAIN check into the generic error path.

-EAGAIN and -ETIMEDOUT both just mean no report was pending at this
instant, the normal steady state for an idle interrupt endpoint, not
a real error. Releasing all keys on every idle poll meant a key that
was still physically held could get force-released the moment any
single poll happened to time out, and an -ETIMEDOUT result additionally
logged disconnect noise and (before a separate fix) killed the poller
outright.

Fix: check for -EAGAIN/-ETIMEDOUT first and exit quietly without
releasing keys or logging, so only a genuine error reaches the
release-and-log path.

Signed-off-by: Stephano Cetola <stephano@cetola.net>
---
 drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c | 7 +++----
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
index 93b55bf72f..d6cb98ac37 100644
--- a/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
+++ b/drivers/input/usb_kbd_hid.c
@@ -100,12 +100,11 @@ static void usb_kbd_poll(void *arg)
 	int ret, i;
 
 	ret = data->do_poll(data);
-	if (ret < 0)
-		usb_kbd_release_all_keys(data);
-	if (ret == -EAGAIN)
+	/* -EAGAIN/-ETIMEDOUT just mean nothing's pending; not a real error. */
+	if (ret == -EAGAIN || ret == -ETIMEDOUT)
 		goto exit;
 	if (ret < 0) {
-		/* exit with noreturn */
+		usb_kbd_release_all_keys(data);
 		dev_err(&usbdev->dev,
 			"usb_submit_int_msg() failed. Keyboard disconnect?\n");
 		goto exit;
